{"type": "step", "node_id": 27, "parent_node_id": 26, "role": "assistant", "content": "## Solution\n\nLet $f(x) = x^{20} - 7x^3 + 1 = \\prod_{i=1}^{20}(x - r_i)$, so $\\dfrac{f'(x)}{f(x)} = \\sum_{i=1}^{20}\\dfrac{1}{x - r_i}$.\n\n**Partial fractions.** Since $\\dfrac{1}{r_i^2+1} = \\dfrac{1}{(r_i-i)(r_i+i)} = \\dfrac{1}{2i}\\!\\left(\\dfrac{1}{r_i-i} - \\dfrac{1}{r_i+i}\\right)$, summing over $i$:\n\n$$\\sum_{i=1}^{20}\\frac{1}{r_i^2+1} = \\frac{1}{2i}\\!\\left(\\sum\\frac{1}{r_i-i} - \\sum\\frac{1}{r_i+i}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2i}\\!\\left(-\\frac{f'(i)}{f(i)} + \\frac{f'(-i)}{f(-i)}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2i}\\!\\left(\\frac{f'(-i)}{f(-i)} - \\frac{f'(i)}{f(i)}\\right).$$\n\n**Evaluate at $x = i$.** With $f'(x) = 20x^{19} - 21x^2$:\n- $i^{20} = 1$, $i^3 = -i$, so $f(i) = 1 - 7(-i) + 1 = 2 + 7i$.\n- $i^{19} = i^{16}\\cdot i^3 = -i$, $i^2 = -1$, so $f'(i) = 20(-i) - 21(-1) = 21 - 20i$.\n\n**Evaluate at $x = -i$.**\n- $(-i)^{20} = 1$, $(-i)^3 = i$, so $f(-i) = 1 - 7i + 1 = 2 - 7i$.\n- $(-i)^{19} = i$, $(-i)^2 = -1$, so $f'(-i) = 20i - 21(-1) = 21 + 20i$.\n\n**Compute the logarithmic derivatives.**\n\n$$\\frac{f'(i)}{f(i)} = \\frac{21-20i}{2+7i}\\cdot\\frac{2-7i}{2-7i} = \\frac{(21-20i)(2-7i)}{53} = \\frac{42 - 187i + 140i^2}{53} = \\frac{-98 - 187i}{53}.$$\n\n$$\\frac{f'(-i)}{f(-i)} = \\frac{21+20i}{2-7i}\\cdot\\frac{2+7i}{2+7i} = \\frac{(21+20i)(2+7i)}{53} = \\frac{42 + 187i + 140i^2}{53} = \\frac{-98 + 187i}{53}.$$\n\n**Take the difference.**\n\n$$\\frac{f'(-i)}{f(-i)} - \\frac{f'(i)}{f(i)} = \\frac{(-98+187i) - (-98-187i)}{53} = \\frac{374i}{53}.$$\n\n**Final sum.**\n\n$$\\sum_{i=1}^{20}\\frac{1}{r_i^2+1} = \\frac{1}{2i}\\cdot\\frac{374i}{53} = \\frac{374}{106} = \\frac{187}{53}.$$\n\n**Coprimality.** $\\gcd(187, 53)$: $187 = 3\\cdot 53 + 28$, $53 = 1\\cdot 28 + 25$, $28 = 1\\cdot 25 + 3$, $25 = 8\\cdot 3 + 1$, so $\\gcd = 1$. Thus $m = 187$, $n = 53$.\n\n$$m + n = 187 + 53 = \\boxed{240}.$$\n\n### PROOF COMPLETE", "thinking": "Let me solve this problem. Let $r_1, \\ldots, r_{20}$ be roots of $f(x) = x^{20} - 7x^3 + 1$. Find $\\sum \\frac{1}{r_i^2+1}$.\n\nLet me use the identity. For a polynomial $f(x) = \\prod (x - r_i)$, we have $\\sum \\frac{1}{r_i^2 + 1} = \\sum \\frac{1}{(r_i - i)(r_i + i)}$.\n\nUsing partial fractions: $\\frac{1}{r_i^2+1} = \\frac{1}{2i}\\left(\\frac{1}{r_i - i} - \\frac{1}{r_i + i}\\right)$.\n\nNow $\\sum \\frac{1}{r_i - a} = \\frac{f'(a)}{f(a)}$... wait, let me be careful. $f(x) = \\prod(x - r_i)$, so $f'(x)/f(x) = \\sum \\frac{1}{x - r_i}$. Thus $\\sum \\frac{1}{r_i - a} = -\\frac{f'(a)}{f(a)}$... Let me check: $\\frac{f'(x)}{f(x)} = \\sum \\frac{1}{x - r_i}$. At $x = a$: $\\sum \\frac{1}{a - r_i} = \\frac{f'(a)}{f(a)}$. So $\\sum \\frac{1}{r_i - a} = -\\frac{f'(a)}{f(a)}$.\n\nSo $\\sum \\frac{1}{r_i^2+1} = \\frac{1}{2i}\\left(\\sum \\frac{1}{r_i - i} - \\sum \\frac{1}{r_i + i}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2i}\\left(-\\frac{f'(i)}{f(i)} + \\frac{f'(-i)}{f(-i)}\\right)$.\n\nWait: $\\sum \\frac{1}{r_i - i} = -\\frac{f'(i)}{f(i)}$ and $\\sum \\frac{1}{r_i + i} = -\\frac{f'(-i)}{f(-i)}$.\n\nSo $\\sum \\frac{1}{r_i^2+1} = \\frac{1}{2i}\\left(-\\frac{f'(i)}{f(i)} + \\frac{f'(-i)}{f(-i)}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2i}\\left(\\frac{f'(-i)}{f(-i)} - \\frac{f'(i)}{f(i)}\\right)$.\n\nNow $f(x) = x^{20} - 7x^3 + 1$, $f'(x) = 20x^{19} - 21x^2$.\n\nCompute $f(i)$: $i^{20} = (i^4)^5 = 1$. $i^3 = -i$. So $f(i) = 1 - 7(-i) + 1 = 2 + 7i$.\n\n$f(-i)$: $(-i)^{20} = 1$. $(-i)^3 = i$. So $f(-i) = 1 - 7i + 1 = 2 - 7i$.\n\n$f'(i) = 20 i^{19} - 21 i^2$. $i^{19} = i^{16} \\cdot i^3 = 1 \\cdot (-i) = -i$. $i^2 = -1$. So $f'(i) = 20(-i) - 21(-1) = 21 - 20i$.\n\n$f'(-i) = 20(-i)^{19} - 21(-i)^2$. $(-i)^{19} = (-i)^{16}(-i)^3 = 1 \\cdot i = i$ (since $(-i)^2 = -1$, $(-i)^4 = 1$, $(-i)^{16}=1$, $(-i)^3 = (-i)^2(-i) = (-1)(-i) = i$). $(-i)^2 = -1$. So $f'(-i) = 20i - 21(-1) = 21 + 20i$.\n\nNow $\\frac{f'(i)}{f(i)} = \\frac{21 - 20i}{2 + 7i}$. Multiply by conjugate: $\\frac{(21-20i)(2-7i)}{(2+7i)(2-7i)} = \\frac{42 - 147i - 40i + 140 i^2}{4 + 49} = \\frac{42 - 187i - 140}{53} = \\frac{-98 - 187i}{53}$.\n\n$\\frac{f'(-i)}{f(-i)} = \\frac{21 + 20i}{2 - 7i}$. Multiply by conjugate: $\\frac{(21+20i)(2+7i)}{(2-7i)(2+7i)} = \\frac{42 + 147i + 40i + 140i^2}{53} = \\frac{42 + 187i - 140}{53} = \\frac{-98 + 187i}{53}$.\n\nSo $\\frac{f'(-i)}{f(-i)} - \\frac{f'(i)}{f(i)} = \\frac{-98 + 187i}{53} - \\frac{-98 - 187i}{53} = \\frac{374i}{53}$.\n\nThus $\\sum \\frac{1}{r_i^2+1} = \\frac{1}{2i} \\cdot \\frac{374i}{53} = \\frac{374}{2 \\cdot 53} = \\frac{187}{53}$.\n\nCheck gcd(187, 53): 53 is prime. 187 = 3·53 + 28, 53 = 1·28 + 25, 28 = 1·25 + 3, 25 = 8·3 + 1. So gcd = 1. Coprime.\n\n$m + n = 187 + 53 = 240$.\n\nLet me double check the computation. $f(i) = i^{20} - 7i^3 + 1 = 1 - 7(-i) + 1 = 2 + 7i$. ✓\n$f(-i) = (-i)^{20} - 7(-i)^3 + 1 = 1 - 7(i) + 1 = 2 - 7i$. ✓\n$f'(i) = 20i^{19} - 21i^2 = 20(-i) - 21(-1) = -20i + 21 = 21 - 20i$. ✓\n$f'(-i) = 20(-i)^{19} - 21(-i)^2 = 20(i) - 21(-1) = 20i + 21 = 21 + 20i$. ✓\n\n$(21-20i)(2-7i) = 42 - 147i - 40i + 140i^2 = 42 - 187i - 140 = -98 - 187i$. ✓\nDenominator $4 + 49 = 53$. ✓\n\n$(21+20i)(2+7i) = 42 + 147i + 40i + 140i^2 = 42 + 187i - 140 = -98 + 187i$. ✓\n\nDifference: $(-98+187i) - (-98-187i) = 374i$. Over 53. ✓\n\n$\\frac{1}{2i} \\cdot \\frac{374i}{53} = \\frac{374}{106} = \\frac{187}{53}$. ✓\n\n$m+n = 240$.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1787239476}
